From 94554d77153b00982d3359377eaadad99a6ec87c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 16:49:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: keep app wraps below the sticky badge renderable

`App._app_root` sorts app wraps by priority descending and appends each
lower-priority wrap as a *child* of the previous one, so every wrap below
the badge lands inside it. The badge wrap was the bare `@memo` component,
whose compiled function `memo(({}) => <a .../>)` never reads
`props.children`, so anything nested under it was emitted into `root.jsx`
and then dropped at render time.

In production with the default `show_built_with_reflex=True` this swallowed
`rx.data_editor`'s `(-1, "DataEditorPortal")` wrap: `<div id="portal">`
never reached the DOM and Glide Data Grid logged "Cannot open Data Grid
overlay editor, because portal not found", so no overlay cell editor --
including the new image-preview carousel -- could open. Dev mode (no badge)
and `show_built_with_reflex=False` were unaffected.

Register the badge wrap as `Fragment.create(memoized_badge())`, the same
shape the toaster and default-overlay wraps already use, so a lower-priority
wrap becomes a sibling of the badge instead of its child.

Fixes #6143

